Provenance
----------

GEOtopPY is a derivative work of GEOtop, translated function by function from
C++ to Python.  It is not an independent reimplementation: numerical
expressions, argument orders, layer index conventions and loop structures are
reproduced deliberately. The port is validated against the original at
explicit numerical tolerances. GPL-3.0 applies to this work as to its source.

  GEOtop
  Copyright (C) 2013 Stefano Endrizzi and the GEOtop contributors
  https://github.com/geotopmodel/geotop
  Licensed under GPL-3.0

The exact revision every translated line refers to is pinned in the UPSTREAM
file at the root of this repository.  Comments of the form
`# GEOtop: src/<path>:<line>` in `src/geotop_py/` cite that revision and are
checked against it by `python -m tools.citations --check`.  Older references
that give only a bare file name and line are being converted to that form;
until then they are not verified, and some do not follow the official tree's
layout.

Third-party material redistributed here
---------------------------------------

`tests/1D/` holds the 13 one-dimensional acceptance cases, copied from
`tests/1D` of the GEOtop repository at the revision pinned in UPSTREAM.  Every
file is byte-for-byte as upstream ships it: inputs, and the `output-tabs-SE27XX`
tables the C++ build produces from them.  The only change is subtraction --
files no case uses (unreferenced forcing series, `.old` copies, the reference
run's own output directory) were left out, which halves the size and changes
nothing a run reads.

  Copyright (C) 2013 Stefano Endrizzi and the GEOtop contributors
  Licensed under GPL-3.0

`tests/data/oracle_replay.json.gz` holds numerical results computed by that same
GEOtop revision -- the answers of 2425 calls, recorded so the port can be
checked against them without building the C++.  Facts about what the program
computes, not its code, but they originate there.
